# PyCharm
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Abstra
# Abstra is an AI-powered process automation framework.
# Ignore directories containing user credentials, local state, and settings.
# Learn more at https://abstra.io/docs
.abstra/

# Visual Studio Code
#  Visual Studio Code specific template is maintained in a separate VisualStudioCode.gitignore 
#  that can be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/VisualStudioCode.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file. However, if you prefer, 
#  you could uncomment the following to ignore the entire vscode folder
# .vscode/

# Ruff stuff:
.ruff_cache/

# PyPI configuration file
.pypirc

# Cursor
#  Cursor is an AI-powered code editor. `.cursorignore` specifies files/directories to
#  exclude from AI features like autocomplete and code analysis. Recommended for sensitive data
#  refer to https://docs.cursor.com/context/ignore-files
.cursorignore
.cursorindexingignore

# Cursor local project state (do not commit)
.cursor/

# Claude Code
#  settings.local.json contains personal/local overrides and should not be shared
.claude/settings.local.json

# Kilo
#  Project config under .kilo/ (agent/*.md, command/*.md) is shareable and stays
#  tracked — do not ignore the whole folder.
#  agent-manager.json is local UI/recovery state. Kilo ships a nested .kilo/.gitignore
#  that hides it but also hides itself, so those rules never reach other clones;
#  mirroring the path here keeps local state out of every clone.
.kilo/agent-manager.json
#  Scratch plan files written by plan mode. Intentional plans belong in
#  docs/superpowers/plans/ (see the SDD note at the bottom of this file).
.kilo/plans/

# Marimo
marimo/_static/
marimo/_lsp/
__marimo__/

# Script-local generated outputs (see README "Local outputs")
train_detector/runs/
# includes vram_estimates.json probe cache
train_detector/weights/
detect_images/detections/

# Local safety copies (e.g. train_detector.py.bak kept beside the rewritten script)
*.bak

# Legacy repo-root training outputs (pre script-local layout)
/runs/

# Local exiftool binaries + metadata dumps. Narrowed on purpose: the documented
# helper exiftool/_Run_exiftool.bat (README "Step 4") stays tracked, and narrowing
# avoids gitignore's can't-re-include-inside-an-excluded-directory trap.
exiftool/exiftool_files/
exiftool/outputs/
exiftool/*.exe
exiftool/README.txt

# Model weights / engines / ONNX — too large for git
*.pt
*.engine
*.onnx

# Dataset files — not part of the code
*.yaml
!requirements*.txt

# Remapped dataset outputs (common local naming)
*_remap/
*_remapped/
*_merged/
*_renamed/

# Internal SDD scratch (briefs/reports/reviews) — never part of the public repo.
.superpowers/sdd/
# Spec/plan write-ups are workflow artifacts too. README carries the operative
# behaviour (tile policy, overlap/NMS thresholds, VRAM probe); the locked-decision
# rationale stays recoverable via `git log -- docs/superpowers`.
docs/superpowers/